Now I see it! The `last_context` structure has `last_token_type[MAX_TOKENS]`, `last_token_int[MAX_TOKENS]`, `last_token_str[MAX_TOKENS]`. The `N_DUP` case:

```c
ctx->lc[cnum].last_ntok = ctx->lc[pnum].last_ntok;
int nc = ctx->lc[cnum].last_ntok ? ctx->lc[cnum].last_ntok : MAX_TOKENS;
memcpy(ctx->lc[cnum].last_token_type, ctx->lc[pnum].last_token_type, nc * sizeof(int));
memcpy(ctx->lc[cnum].last_token_int , ctx->lc[pnum].last_token_int , nc * sizeof(int));
memcpy(ctx->lc[cnum].last_token_str , ctx->lc[pnum].last_token_str , nc * sizeof(int));
```

If `ctx->lc[pnum].last_ntok` is uninitialized garbage (e.g., a huge value), then `nc` is huge, and the `memcpy` calls would overflow the `last_token_type`, `last_token_int`, and `last_token_str` arrays. This could corrupt the heap, leading to a double-free.

But wait, `last_ntok` is set in the `N_END` case:
```c
case N_END:
    if (len+1 >= name_len) return -1;
    name[len++] = 0;
    ctx->lc[cnum].last_token_type[ntok] = N_END;
    ctx->lc[cnum].last_name = name;
    ctx->lc[cnum].last_ntok = ntok;
    return len;
```

So `last_ntok` is set when a name is fully decoded. If `pnum`'s name was never decoded (e.g., `pnum` is 0 and `lc[0].last_ntok` was never set), then `last_ntok` is uninitialized.

The fix adds `ctx->lc[0].last_ntok = 0;` in `create_context` and `ctx->lc[cnum].last_ntok = 0;` at the start of the token loop in `decode_name`. This ensures `last_ntok` is always initialized.

But actually, the `N_DUP` case checks `if (pnum == cnum) return -1;`. So `pnum < cnum`. If `pnum` is 0 and `lc[0].last_ntok` was never set (because the first name was never decoded), then `last_ntok` is uninitialized.

Wait, but `cnum` starts at 0. So the first call to `decode_name` has `cnum = 0`. If `t0 == N_DUP`, then `pnum = cnum - dist`. Since `dist > 0` (checked by `dist > cnum`), `pnum < cnum`. If `cnum = 0`, then `dist > 0` means `dist > 0`, and `pnum = 0 - dist < 0`, so `pnum = 0` (clamped). Then `pnum == cnum == 0`, so `return -1`. So the first name can't be a DUP.

For `cnum = 1`, `pnum` could be 0. If `lc[0].last_ntok` was never set (because the first name decode failed or was a DUP), then `last_ntok` is uninitialized.

